6. Falsification protocol

All thresholds are [T]: pre-registered before the first run. No test has been executed. KT tests are named to avoid confusion with K obligations.

6.1 Rules

· Burn-in first. No inference benchmark before the 72-hour platform burn-in, and no burn-in before Phase 0.5 (§8.1) has produced a tethered-rig latency measurement.
· Pinned and logged. Engine, CUDA, driver, model versions pinned. Both clocks, queue depths, service times, link RTT, power, temperature logged.
· Report tails, not means. p50, p95, p99, p99.9, max, with sample size.
· Zero-failure sample sizes. 299 independent trials bound failure at ~1% with 95% confidence (0.99²⁹⁹ = 0.0495) [C]. This does not certify a hazard rate.
· Kill, do not rescue. A failed threshold triggers the stated consequence, not a new threshold.
· Label the claim. Every test is performance or model validation. The structural claim rests on B0's deterministic check, not on a trial count.

